This is something that can't be found from the Properties tab, so pivoting information sources is necessary. 
Exiftool can read and write metadata that maybe isn't shown in the Properties. Syntax is:
exiftool -f [file]
Where the -f switch forces the command to output all tags. I had to look this one up, as just running "exiftool [file]" does not give us any comments.
